  <h1>TAMU-CAT Overview and User Guide</h1>
  <p>Texas A&amp;M University Competency Assessment Tool</p>
</div>

<h2>Purpose</h2>
<p>TAMU-CAT collects competency assessment information across the MHA program and presents it as student, advisor, faculty, and program-level evidence.</p>

<h2>Who uses TAMU-CAT?</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Primary activities</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Student</td><td>Complete assigned competency surveys, provide portfolio evidence, review results, and download personal records.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Advisor</td><td>Review student competency information, record academic/career/general meeting notes, and monitor advisees.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Faculty and administrator</td><td>Import course assessments, review missing data, configure targets, and analyze results by track and cohort.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Typical workflow</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Configure program tracks, semesters, cohorts, competency targets, and survey questions.</li>
  <li>Assign the appropriate survey to students by track and graduating class.</li>
  <li>Students complete the assigned survey and submit portfolio evidence.</li>
  <li>Faculty data is imported through the admin grade-import workflow, including a review step before commit.</li>
  <li>Advisors review student results and complete the meeting recap fields.</li>
  <li>Administrators use Reports to review achievement at program and course targets by track and cohort.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Reports and exports</h2>
<p>The Reports page provides filters, charts, cohort comparisons, course-target attainment, heatmaps, student profile exports, PDF output, and cohort-specific PDF bundles.</p>
<p>Course-derived ratings remain separate from student self-assessments and advisor feedback. A program report may show <strong>0 / Not able to assess</strong> when an assessment cannot be compared; this value is not a failure and is excluded from achieved/not-achieved percentages.</p>

<h2>Data quality and privacy</h2>
<p>Use the grade-import review page to resolve missing assessments and missing course targets before relying on reports. Reports can contain student education records. Download and share them only for legitimate educational purposes and store them securely.</p>

<h2>Support</h2>
<p>For survey assignment or cohort setup, contact the program administrator. For application behavior, imports, or report generation, contact the TAMU-CAT support team.</p>